~ start
The Guardian: It looks like a forest of stone... The air whistles without harmony here.
The Guardian: Look at these monumental structures. Something important was broken here.
=> END

~ indice_stele
The Guardian: "From the rumbling of the earth to the whistling of the summit."
The Guardian: That means from longest to shortest. From Low pitch to High pitch.
=> END

~ lecon_inca
Incan Spirit: Stranger, my soul wanders because my sacred Syrinx has been scattered by the silence.
Incan Spirit: I need your help to reconstruct its voice, from the deepest breath to the highest whisper.
Incan Spirit: Remember the law of the Andes: a long tube holds the air and sings Low; a short tube releases it quickly and sings High.
Incan Spirit: Gather the five pipes in order, from the longest to the shortest, to restore the harmony.
=> END

~ success
The Guardian: Listen! The air is flowing perfectly through the tubes.
Incan Spirit: You have repaired my flute! The sacred scale echoes once again in the mountains.
=> END

~ suite_success
Wind Spirit: *Fuuuushhh... Shhh...* Thank you, creators of wind. The harmony is reclaimed!
The Guardian: The melody is pure... the final passage is open!
=> END